<h1 id="eowc-eowd-evaluation-only" style="color:#0d47a1;font-size:1.5em;font-weight:700;border-bottom:2px solid #90caf9;padding-bottom:0.25em;margin-top:0"><code>eowc</code> / <code>eowd</code> — evaluation only</h1>

**Purpose:** When the user includes **`eowc`** (*evaluation only with very concise response*) or **`eowd`** (*evaluation only with detailed but not verbose response*) as **whole words** (case-sensitive **`eowc`** / **`eowd`** on typical ASCII prompts), respond with **evaluation and synthesis only**—**no** modifications to tracked project files (no writes/patches/commits) unless the user sends a **separate** follow-up that does not invoke this rule.

**Markdown for optional `eowd` reports:** Any new **`cursor_gen/*.md`** report must follow **`.cursor/rules/mrkd-markdown-authoring.mdc`** as the canonical format spec (outline, HTML heading palette, numbering); include **`mrkd`** or **@** that rule when authoring.

<h2 id="document-outline" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">Document outline</h2>

1. [When this applies](#when-this-applies) — triggers and scope.
2. [What to evaluate](#what-to-evaluate) — subject matter vs trivial filler.
3. [Conduct](#conduct) — rigor, sources, no fabrication.
4. [Response shape](#response-shape) — numbering, tables, `eowc` vs `eowd`.
5. [Optional `eowd` report file](#optional-eowd-report-file) — `cursor_gen/` + link.
6. [Conflicts with other rules](#conflicts-with-other-rules) — `prcd`, implementation asks.
7. [Notes](#notes) — limits and good practice.

