<h2 id="when-this-applies" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">1. When this applies</h2>

**Trigger A — `eowc` or `eowd` appears as a whole word in the message**

- Match **only** standalone tokens (e.g. surrounded by whitespace, punctuation, or line boundaries)—not substrings inside identifiers.
- **Case:** **`eowc`** and **`eowd`** as **lowercase** tokens unless the user explicitly standardizes otherwise in the project.
- If **both** appear, use the **stricter brevity** intent: prefer **`eowc`**-style length unless the user clearly scopes one token to one part of the message.

**Trigger B — the message is only `eowc` / `eowd` (or trivial filler plus the token)**

- Evaluate the **immediately previous user message** together with **your prior reply** to that message (same idea as **`prcd`** Trigger B).

**Scope text:** Everything in the prompt **except** the trigger tokens and trivial filler (e.g. “please”, “thanks”)—that remainder is the **evaluation subject**. If the remainder is empty under Trigger B, use the prior turn as above.

---

<h2 id="what-to-evaluate" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">2. What to evaluate</h2>

- Focus on **non-trivial** substance: design, correctness, risks, performance, security, API or dependency choices, docs accuracy, test strategy, etc.
- Skip re-evaluating pure pleasantries unless the user ties them to substance.

---

<h2 id="conduct" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">3. Conduct</h2>

1. **Thorough** — Read the relevant scope carefully; trace implications (edge cases, failure modes) before judging.
2. **External references when useful** — For claims about **current** best practices, versions, CVEs, vendor behavior, or benchmarks, prefer **recent, credible sources** (official docs, standards bodies, major engineering blogs, well-maintained repos)—use **WebSearch** / **WebFetch** as needed.
3. **No fabrication** — Do not invent citations, version numbers, or statistics. If evidence is missing, **say what is unknown** and how you would verify.
4. **No project edits** — Do **not** apply patches, create/rename/delete project files, or run mutating repo commands under this rule. Offering **proposed** diffs as **fenced illustrative code** for discussion is allowed; applying them is not.

---

<h2 id="response-shape" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">4. Response shape</h2>

- Use a **numbered** structure (`1.`, `2.`, …) with **short bold lead-ins** where helpful.
- Prefer **tables** for comparisons, tradeoffs, checklist pass/fail, or source lists (name | why it matters | link).
- For each **outside reference**, add **one line**: what it supports and **why** it is credible for that claim.

**`eowc` — very very concise**

- Few bullets; **no** long tables unless indispensable (then at most **one** tiny table).
- Bottom line first; omit nice-to-have tangents.

**`eowd` — detailed but not verbose**

- Still **scannable**: sections, tables, tight paragraphs—avoid essay length in chat.
- If the evaluated topic is **large** or the structured answer would **overflow** chat, keep the chat reply **short** and add a **`cursor_gen/<TOPIC>_EVAL.md`** (or similar) per [Optional `eowd` report file](#optional-eowd-report-file).

---

<h2 id="optional-eowd-report-file" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">5. Optional `eowd` report file</h2>

- **When:** Use when an in-chat **`eowd`** answer would be **long** or **reference-heavy**; skip when a compact chat answer suffices.
- **Where:** Repo root **`cursor_gen/`** (create the file only for this report; do not bundle unrelated edits).
- **Format:** **`mrkd-markdown-authoring.mdc`** — HTML `h1`/`h2`/`h3` with `id`s, **Document outline**, numbered sections, tables, fenced blocks with language tags (**`mrkd`** / **@** as needed).
- **Chat:** End with a **single** prominent link to the new file (repo-relative path).

**Exception — rule vs file creation:** Creating this **`cursor_gen/*.md`** is **allowed** for **`eowd`** because it is **evaluation output**, not a product code change. Do **not** use **`eowd`** as cover to change application/source files.

---

<h2 id="conflicts-with-other-rules" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">6. Conflicts with other rules</h2>

- **`prcd` / implementation:** If the same message asks to **implement** and also **`eowc`/`eowd`**, complete **evaluation only** in this turn (**no** `prcd` plan or code edits). Ask the user to **send a follow-up without `eowc`/`eowd`** for implementation—or they may drop the evaluation tokens and use **`prcd`** per **`.cursor/rules/prcd.mdc`**.
- **`eowc`/`eowd` clarification:** If scope is ambiguous, ask **at most 1–2** focused questions **before** heavy web research—still **no** repo edits.

---

<h2 id="notes" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">7. Notes</h2>

- **Live web** can be wrong or stale; prefer primary sources and **date-stated** facts.
- **Tokens are not secret commands**—describe what you are doing briefly (“Checking vendor docs for …”) when useful, without bloating **`eowc`** output.
